      "exampleEnglish": "I will wait at the station before the train.",
      "grammarNote": "A closing capstone for levels 61-70: the سَـ-future (level 41) built on أَنْتَظِرُ ('I wait', Form VIII, level 63), placed فِي الْمَحَطَّةِ ('at the station', level 68), followed by قَبْلَ الْقِطَارِ ('before the train', level 67 preposition + level 68 vocabulary). 70 of 100 levels now authored. أَحْيَانًا ('sometimes') joins the small -ًا adverb family (غَدًا, جِدًّا, أَيْضًا, قَلِيلًا, دَائِمًا) with a fittingly-timed opposite of دَائِمًا (level 60, 'always').",
